@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.LetsSignItCornerModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Let’s Sign It Corner";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Workshops">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <!-- HERO -->
        <div class="kbi-hero reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Workshops & Learning</p>
                <h2>Let’s Sign It! Corner</h2>
                <p>
                    Where hands speak louder than words — a weekly corner at Car Free Day
                    Malang where people pause, learn, play, and connect through sign language.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-hero.jpg" alt="Let’s Sign It Corner">
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 1 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>A Space to Pause and Connect</h3>
                <p>
                    Every week at Car Free Day in Malang, we create a small corner
                    in the middle of the crowd.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Not to stand out, but to invite people to pause—even just for a moment—
                    and experience something different.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Through this corner, we share a glimpse into the Deaf world,
                    not through explanation, but through experience.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Some people simply pass by. Some stop out of curiosity.
                    And some choose to stay. That is where it begins.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reverse reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-learn-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-learn-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-learn-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Learning Comes First</h3>
                <p>
                    For us, it was never about winning or losing.
                    It has always been about the process.
                </p>
                <p>
                    We invite people to start with the basics—learning the alphabet,
                    simple words, and the first steps of sign language.
                </p>
                <p>
                    At the beginning, it feels unfamiliar. Hands move awkwardly,
                    and gestures feel unsure.
                </p>
                <p>
                    But slowly, almost without realizing it, something shifts.
                    They begin to understand a different way of communicating.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-game-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-game-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-game-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Game with Purpose</h3>
                <p>
                    After learning, the experience continues through simple games
                    designed not just to be fun, but to carry meaning.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The roulette sets the level of challenge. From there, participants
                    interact directly with our Deaf baristas, trying to read, guess,
                    and understand the signs given.
                </p>
                <p>
                    When they succeed, they move on to the ring toss—a small challenge
                    that requires focus, timing, and a bit of patience.
                </p>
                <p>
                    But more than the game itself, we value the moment when something
                    finally makes sense.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 4 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reverse reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-gift-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-gift-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">
                <img src="/images/LetsSignItCorner/lsi-gift-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide" alt="">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Small Gifts, Bigger CINTA</h3>
                <p>
                    The small gifts we prepare—stickers, keychains, and other simple
                    merchandise—are never just rewards.
                </p>
                <p>
                    They are a way of appreciating the experience, the effort,
                    and the new perspective someone carries after spending time
                    at our corner.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Through this campaign, we want to share Deaf awareness in a way
                    that feels real and easy to connect with.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- CLOSING -->
        <div class="detail-section reveal" style="text-align:center;">
            <h3>CINTA Does Not Always Need to Be Spoken</h3>
            <p>
                If one day you find us there, don’t hesitate to stop.
                You might walk away with something more than just a game.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Workshops" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Workshops</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>